cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite the MSc thesis below."
title: >-
  MSc Thesis Defence — Development of a GIS Application for the Automatic
  Classification of Multispectral & Thermal UAV Images Using Convolutional
  Neural Networks
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Koroniadis
    given-names: Nikolaos
    affiliation: "University of the Aegean — Department of Geography"
abstract: >-
  Bilingual (EN/EL), offline reveal.js presentation for an MSc thesis comparing
  a 7-band (multispectral + nDSM + thermal) versus an RGB semantic-segmentation
  pipeline (DeepLabV3 + PointRend / ResNet-101) on UAV imagery of Pamfila,
  Lesvos (GSD 4.52 cm). The advantage is shown to be driven by geometry (nDSM)
  and heat (LWIR) rather than spectrum.
keywords:
  - remote sensing
  - semantic segmentation
  - convolutional neural networks
  - UAV
  - multispectral
  - thermal
  - nDSM
  - DeepLabV3
  - PointRend
  - GIS
